Spec 17 Part F: GDI objects that 32-bit programs share with the session. F1: one inline
function in win32u_private.h answers the allocation ceiling (zero_bits expands to it), and
NtGdiCreateDIBSection maps a caller's section with it. F4: the handle table is published in the
caller's PEB before any handle-table operation (handle_entry, alloc_gdi_handle, alloc_dc_attr;
w32ios_mem.c). F5/F6: DC attribute buckets and cache DCEs carry their creator, and in a 32-bit
session serve only their own process when either side is 32-bit (w32ios_s17_pure.c).
Applied after spec 12's patches.

